Not bad at all, especially given that it's your first time past level
8. Did you make a high score?

Some things you could have considered:
o Your equipment was at rather low enchantments. With the charges left
in your magic marker you could have gotten that hammer up to +6 or +7,
or your armor up some more, too.
o Instead of using melee on the Riders, you should probably have used
up all of your offensive wands first. Maybe you could have tried using
that otherwise useless Demonbane against them?
o You were level 17 when you left the dungeon? That's impressive, but
with your max HP below 200, you probably would have lasted longer if
you had stayed and trained a bit more. Did the VotD yield wraith
corpses? Gaining levels are a priority if you're about to descend into
Gehennom.
o Equipment is very important. Understandably, you lost a lot of items
when your bag blew, but it's a good idea to keep a = of Free Action and
a = of Conflict in your inventory at all times.
o What unnecessary items did you have? You should keep all of your
useful items in your inventory and the junk in your bags. You could
have dropped the duplicate = of Levitation, your uncursed luckstone
(the Orb of Fate acts as one), and the cursed unicorn horn whenever you
got them, and things like the lizard corpse and the ring of teleport
control once you were in the astral plane, though it's not nearly as
important then.

Overall, it was a very good run, and better luck next time!



